---
import Section from './Section.astro'
// Facts checked against vippsas/manifold: resources/plugins/* manifests and
// docs/architecture/plugins.md.
//
// The privileged capabilities (agent:control, agent:spawn, lm, workspace:manage,
// verdicts:*, transcription:read) are restricted to BUILT-IN plugins regardless
// of what a manifest claims. That is precisely why an enterprise plugin needing
// them has to come through us. Say that plainly rather than implying anyone can
// self-serve a privileged plugin.
const shipped = [
  { id: 'manifold.loop', name: 'Loop', desc: 'Edit → evaluate → keep or discard.' },
  { id: 'manifold.statistics', name: 'Statistics', desc: 'Per-runtime quality metrics across every repository.' },
  { id: 'manifold.worktrees', name: 'Worktrees', desc: 'Every managed worktree, in one view.' },
  { id: 'manifold.watch', name: 'Watch', desc: 'Hand the agent a video: frames, transcript, report.' },
]
---
<Section id="plugins" eyebrow="Plugins">
  <Fragment slot="title">Extend it with <em>your own tooling</em>.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Manifold's own features are plugins. The automated Loop is one of them, so the
    extension model is the one we build on ourselves.
  </Fragment>

  <ul class="grid">
    {shipped.map((p) => (
      <li>
        <span class="name">{p.name}</span>
        <code>{p.id}</code>
        <span class="desc">{p.desc}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="body">
    Your own plugins load from <code>~/.manifold/plugins</code>. Each one runs in a
    sandboxed host process, not in the app's main process and not in the UI, and declares
    the capabilities it needs in its manifest. The host enforces that list. An unrecognised
    capability rejects the whole manifest rather than being quietly ignored, so a typo can't
    widen a plugin's reach.
  </p>

  <div class="mono-figure boxed">
    <pre>  <b>manifest</b>     declares capabilities   <span class="dim">storage · workspace:read · configuration</span>
  <b>host</b>         forks a sandboxed process, brokers every call
  <b>gate</b>         unknown capability → <span class="dim">whole manifest rejected</span>
  <b>privileged</b>   agent:control · agent:spawn · lm · workspace:manage
               <span class="dim">built-in only, whatever a manifest claims</span></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="body">
    Plugin ids can't contain a path separator, per-plugin storage is escape-guarded, and
    plugin webviews are served over their own scheme under a nonce CSP. There is also a
    VS&nbsp;Code compatibility shim, so a subset of existing extensions runs unmodified:
    commands, activation events and tree views.
  </p>

  <div class="caveat">
    <p>
      <b>For enterprises.</b> Plugins that read the workspace, keep their own state or
      contribute views, your team can write and drop in yourself. Three capabilities stay
      reserved for built-in plugins, whatever a manifest asks for: driving an agent,
      spawning one, and reaching the language model. Those we build together. Bring the use
      case, and what ships lands as a built-in under the same MIT licence.
      <a href="/enterprise">How that works</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    display: grid;
    /* Four shipped plugins; 215px lets all four sit on one row at full width
       rather than leaving the fourth alone on a second. */
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(215px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }
  .grid li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-gold);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--frame-highlight);
  }
  .name { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .grid code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .desc { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.88rem; margin-top: var(--space-xs); }

  .body { color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .body code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--accent-cyan); }

  .caveat {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-cyan);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--frame-highlight);
  }
  .caveat p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .caveat b { color: var(--text-primary); }
</style>
